      "message": "There are 3 conditions that terminate the loop, a success condition and 2 error conditions. Rather that putting a condition in the while statement that needs to be checked for when the loop exits again to determine if an error occurred, all 3 conditions are checked for in the loop body, one error in the try/except segment, one in the expiration of the counter, and the success again in the try/except. Putting a single one of these in the wile condition might cause the code to be misread in the future as the only terminating condition.",
